  "body": "## What changed\n\nMain is red on `corner_arc_radius` (\"Waterline: no corner turned on an arc\"). PR #2273 sent the rounded walks of Waterline and Offset rings through `post_crossing_free`. That law maps a crossing arc onto the vertices of the pass. A rounded walk has new vertices, so one hit gave the whole pass back to plain chords.\n\nThis PR changes the law for corner arcs only. The decision is in `docs/decisions/2317-blend-crossing-law.md`.\n\n1. `machining2d/blend_cross.rs` (new): the law keeps the walks as fitted and rounds them again each round.\n   - A corner arc that crosses another feed bans its own corner. The corner stays sharp. The fillet note counts it: \"an arc there would cross another feed\".\n   - A fitted arc that crosses goes back to the chords of the plan, through `arc_cross::refuse` on the fitted walks.\n   - After `CROSS_ROUNDS` (3) rounds no corner is rounded and the classic law holds on the fitted walks.\n2. `machining2d/arc_touch.rs` (new): a tangent touch of a corner arc is not a crossing. A chord `q` is a touch when it stays within `d` of the tangent line at an end of the arc, over the reach of the bracket, and `d + dr <= 1e-5 mm`. `dr` is the difference of the two end radii.\n3. `machining2d/fillet.rs`: `fillet_corners_except` takes the banned corners and returns the trace of each added or trimmed arc. `fillet_corners` is a wrapper with no ban.\n4. `machining2d/pocket_emit.rs`: with corner arcs on and the law in force, the pocket calls the new loop.\n\n## Proof bound of the touch\n\nA circle lies on one side of each of its tangents. The last edge of the circumscribed hull lies on the tangent at the end. Thus each bracket point `X` holds `(X - E) . n <= dr`. Thus the true arc passes `q` by `d + dr <= 1e-5 mm` at most. The allowance can hide no crossing deeper than 0.01 micrometer. A pair that cannot be measured (no finite radius, an empty clip, a NaN) is a crossing.\n\nA tolerance in the general predicate was dropped: it has no proof bound at a shared vertex. Adaptive (HSM) and `machining3d::hsm` pass an empty set of corner arcs, so their result is the same as before.\n\n## Readings\n\nFixture of `corner_arc_radius` (pocket with an island, 8 mm tool):\n\n| Case | Corner arcs kept | Corners refused for a crossing | `crossed_pairs` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Waterline, 1 mm | 12 of 31 | 0 | empty |\n| Waterline, tool radius | 22 of 45 | 4 | empty |\n| Offset rings, 1 mm | 35 of 38 | 0 | empty |\n| Offset rings, tool radius | 31 of 38 | 0 | empty |\n\nWithout the touch allowance (experiment, not committed): 1 Waterline corner and 2 Offset rings corners at 1 mm lose their arc for a touch.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests in `crates/motion/tests/corner_arc_radius.rs`:\n\n- `the_crossing_law_keeps_the_arc_turns_and_crosses_nowhere` (new)\n- `corners_turn_on_tangent_arcs_of_the_given_radius` (now reports each strategy that fails)\n- unit tests `only_a_chord_on_the_end_tangent_is_a_touch` and `a_radius_mismatch_past_the_bound_leaves_no_touch` in `arc_touch.rs`\n\nRun on head `79ea4410d22bda122207e9624123c31bfedd95fb`, debug, all pass:\n\n- `camcraft-motion --lib` (405), `corner_arc_radius` (8), `corner_blend` (14), `corner_blend_arc` (9), `corner_blend_arc_contour` (1), `machining2d` (68), `rest2d` (13), `rest_zigzag` (2), `level_links` (12), `xy_arc_entry` (5), `entry_arc` (12)\n- HSM and Adaptive: `adaptive_band` (2), `adaptive_hsm` (2), `adaptive_orbit_seam` (1), `pocket3d_hsm` (3), `pocket3d_mask_edge` (4), `machining3d` (23), `cross_invariance` (2), `optimal_load` (4), `pocket_refusal` (3), `predrilled_entry` (6)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- `camcraft-app --test golden_cl` (33): pass, no golden moved\n\n## Output that changes\n\nPocket operations with corner arcs on, with strategy Waterline or Offset rings (also as the fallback of Adaptive), or with `hold_crossings`: the corner arcs are back, less the corners that would cross. With corner arcs off, nothing changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The ignored (release lane) tests.\n- The UI and the post processors. The bound is stated against the 1e-6 mm lattice of the CL data. The word format of each post script was not read.\n- The fallback after `CROSS_ROUNDS` has no fixture that reaches it.\n- Zigzag and Auto without `hold_crossings` post rounded walks with no crossing law, as before #2273. This PR does not change that.\n\nChangelog: Pocket corner arcs are back for Waterline and Offset rings; a corner whose arc would cross another feed stays sharp and the note says so (#2317).\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #2317\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
